  "notes": [
    {
      "attrs": {},
      "author": null,
      "body": "The user explicitly canceled the four unfinished FineMath targets (30%, 50%, 70%, 100%) on 12 September UTC. Iris confirms all four are KILLED. Their latest checkpoints at steps 7965, 6426, 7219 and 6432 were preserved with generation-pinned, create-only server-side copies within marin-us-central1, outside the temporary lifecycle prefix. All 28 checkpoint objects (10,164,798,257 bytes) match in size, CRC32C and MD5; checkpoint metadata and relative object sets also match. See checkpoint_preservation_receipt.json for exact durable paths and source/destination generations.\n\nAll 14 proxy points and 10 target points remain successful. Both audit workers remain successful and all three numerical audit receipts remain valid. After verifying every child was terminal, stop requests were issued for the idle survey and repair coordinators. Their final Iris states are FAILED and KILLED respectively; neither tree contains active or queued jobs. No new training or evaluation was submitted.\n\nFurther target training requires a separate explicit user promotion after proxy analysis. Do not retry these four cancellations, either parent, or the old recovery plan automatically. The stopped repair coordinator assumed all 28 training points would succeed, so native artifact-record recovery remains incomplete; completing those records for the 24 finished points must not retrain or fabricate success for the canceled points. Corrected immutable result snapshots and the completed checkpoints remain available.\n\nThe original discussion was proxy-first. The later request to locate optima in both target and matched settings expanded the reviewed and submitted scope; this was not reconciled with the original staging gate before launch. Current scope is proxy analysis with target expansion deferred. Central1 MATH-500 (500 examples) and GSM8K (1,319 examples) are confirmed available as raw evaluation data; no math results have yet been measured on these checkpoints.\n",
      "body_format": "markdown",
